    "name": "zoom_box_busi_v1",
    "locked_at": "2026-10-06",
    "purpose": "Evaluation-only control on breast ultrasound. On polyps (zoom_box_v1) a plain crop of twice the predicted box was not distinguishable from the locked window rule. The rule, however, takes its magnification from the training masks of each source dataset (quantile matching, target fraction 0.086 for BUSI), whereas a fixed factor has to be chosen. Question: does the factor that was best on polyps (2.0) transfer to ultrasound, or does the rule, which was not tuned on ultrasound either, do better there? Nothing is trained; the locked configuration remains the method whatever the outcome, and the outcome is reported whatever it is.",
    "locked_before": "Written after zoom_box_v1 (polyps) had been accepted and before any box-crop result on ultrasound existed.",
